Diagnostic only: with -Dwj.asyncReport (TeaVM reads build properties from the JVM's), the linear-memory wasm target
prints every reachable suspending (@Async) method and a caller chain to the first method outside java.* and
org.teavm.*. Any such method makes TeaVM coroutine-transform its transitive callers, which mctick's TeaVM arm must
not have (bench/teavm-classlib/src/wjteavm/Background.java). Codegen: none.

